course: dictionary
lesson: 8997
title: Skateboard: a thing and an action
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can be a thing or an action, depending on how it is used. «Skateboard wheels and bearings have little friction» uses skateboard as a thing, the board you stand on. Words like skateboards, skateboarding and skateboarded show that the action is happening or happened.
explain: Context clues help here. «Skateboard wheels and bearings have little friction, so a smooth path keeps you rolling, but small wheels catch on gravel.» The sentence talks about wheels, paths and gravel, so skateboard must be the board with wheels, not a sport or a trick.
explain: The context also shows safety. «Wrist guards and helmets protect against the falls» tells you that skateboarding can be risky, so you wear protection and ride away from traffic.
explain: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence. «Ella will skateboard in the park tomorrow» becomes «Ella will ride a skateboard in the park tomorrow», and it still makes sense, so skateboard here means to ride one.
fact: A skateboard is a narrow board with four small wheels, which you stand on.
fact: To skateboard means to ride a skateboard, pushing with one foot.
fact: Skateboarding is also an Olympic sport.
fact: Where there is little friction, motion lasts: «a skateboard on a smooth path rolls on and on after one push».
fact: Forces come in pairs: when you push a heavy ball forward on a skateboard, the ball pushes you backwards just as hard.
exercise: In «Ella will skateboard in the park tomorrow», what does skateboard mean? | A helmet with pads | A smooth path away from traffic | *To ride a skateboard | A narrow board with four wheels
exercise: «A skateboard on a smooth path rolls on and on after one push.» Why does it keep rolling? | Gravel catches the wheels | It has a small motor inside it | Wrist guards push it along | *Little friction slows it down only a little
exercise: Why do skaters wear wrist guards? | They make the board go faster | They remove friction from the wheels | *They protect the wrist from breaking when a hand is thrown out in a fall | They are only worn in the Olympics
test: Which phrase names a place to skate? | do tricks | ride a skateboard | *skate park | wrist guard
test: What does «Forces come in pairs» mean? | Skaters always ride in pairs | Forces are always very large | Friction never happens | *Each push gets an equal push back
exam: Ella swaps her old scooter for her neighbour's skateboard, and both feel they got the better deal. What is this kind of swap called? | A friction pair | A broken wrist | A skate park | *A win-win swap
